{
  "id": "m14l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Buscar patrones con re",
    "en": "Searching patterns with re"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Patrones de texto"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "El módulo `re` busca **patrones** en texto. Atajos útiles: `\\d` = un dígito, `\\w` = letra/dígito/_, `+` = uno o más, `*` = cero o más, `.` = cualquier carácter."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import re",
          "print(re.search(r'\\d+', 'abc123'))",
          "print(bool(re.search(r'\\d', 'hola')))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "<re.Match object; span=(3, 6), match='123'>",
          "False"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`re.findall(patron, texto)` devuelve **todas** las coincidencias en una lista. Usa cadenas 'raw' (`r'...'`) para escribir los patrones sin pelearte con las barras."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import re",
          "print(re.findall(r'\\d+', 'tengo 2 gatos y 3 perros'))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "['2', '3']"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Las regex son potentísimas para validar entradas y analizar logs (clave en ciberseguridad), pero se vuelven ilegibles rápido: úsalas con cabeza."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Text patterns"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "The `re` module searches for **patterns** in text. Handy shortcuts: `\\d` = a digit, `\\w` = letter/digit/_, `+` = one or more, `*` = zero or more, `.` = any character."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import re",
          "print(re.search(r'\\d+', 'abc123'))",
          "print(bool(re.search(r'\\d', 'hola')))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "<re.Match object; span=(3, 6), match='123'>",
          "False"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`re.findall(pattern, text)` returns **all** matches in a list. Use 'raw' strings (`r'...'`) to write patterns without fighting backslashes."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import re",
          "print(re.findall(r'\\d+', 'tengo 2 gatos y 3 perros'))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "['2', '3']"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Regex are powerful for validating input and parsing logs (key in security), but get unreadable fast: use them wisely."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m14l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `tiene_numero(texto)` que devuelva True si el texto contiene algún dígito (usa `re.search`).",
        "en": "Define `tiene_numero(texto)` returning True if the text contains any digit (use `re.search`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import re",
        "",
        "def tiene_numero(texto):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import re",
        "",
        "def tiene_numero(texto):",
        "    return bool(re.search(r'\\d', texto))"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "re.search(r'\\d', texto) y conviértelo a bool."
        ],
        "en": [
          "re.search(r'\\d', texto) and convert it to bool."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "tiene_numero",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "abc1"
              ],
              "expected": true
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "abc"
              ],
              "expected": false
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "2023"
              ],
              "expected": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m14l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `extraer_numeros(texto)` que devuelva la lista de todos los grupos de dígitos (usa `re.findall(r'\\d+', ...)`).",
        "en": "Define `extraer_numeros(texto)` returning the list of all digit groups (use `re.findall(r'\\d+', ...)`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import re",
        "",
        "def extraer_numeros(texto):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import re",
